# Configuration 9 -- ten thousand smelters fighting over one ore bay.
#
#   MinerA x20 --\                      /-- SmelterA x6000 --\
#   MinerB x20 ----> OreBay ------------                      >-- PlateBay --> Shipping x25
#   MinerC x20 --/                      \-- SmelterB x4000 --/
#
# Every smelter is coupled to every other smelter through OreBay: ore one takes
# is ore the rest cannot have. v1's compression argument does not survive this
# for a second, because nothing here is independent of anything else.
#
# Three miner classes on deliberately mismatched periods (20, 24, 30) so ore
# arrives at 55 different ticks in every 600, rather than in one synchronised
# lump. That matters: it is what spreads the smelters across many different
# phases of their cycle instead of marching them in lockstep, and a spread
# population is the case the compression has to survive.
#
# Supply is 250 ore/tick against 500 ore/tick of smelting capacity, so the two
# smelter classes are permanently short and OreBay has to divide the shortfall
# between them every tick. Two populous classes contending under a declared
# policy is the whole v2 problem in one storage.
#
# Arithmetic: 10,000 smelters, ~25 starting per tick, cycles 200-300 ticks
# long, so roughly 6,000 are mid-cycle at any instant and the rest are queued.
# The mid-cycle ones fall into a few dozen distinct finish ticks, and the
# queued ones are all in one state. A few dozen cells for ten thousand machines.
#
# Deliberately small enough to materialise machine by machine, because this is
# where the lumped solver gets checked against the truth.

item IronOre
item IronPlate

blueprint OreRush {
    source  MinerA x20 { produces 100 IronOre every 20 ticks }
    source  MinerB x20 { produces 100 IronOre every 24 ticks }
    source  MinerC x20 { produces 100 IronOre every 30 ticks }

    storage OreBay { capacity 50000  policy round_robin }

    process SmelterA x6000 { consumes 10 IronOre takes 200 ticks produces 10 IronPlate }
    process SmelterB x4000 { consumes 15 IronOre takes 300 ticks produces 15 IronPlate }

    storage PlateBay { capacity 50000  policy round_robin }
    sink    Shipping x25 { consumes 100 IronPlate every 10 ticks }

    wire MinerA -> OreBay
    wire MinerB -> OreBay
    wire MinerC -> OreBay

    wire OreBay -> SmelterA -> PlateBay
    wire OreBay -> SmelterB -> PlateBay
    wire PlateBay -> Shipping
}

deploy 1 x OreRush
